codex
Implemented and verified a native Track B finite-field polynomial family based on the paper’s explicit local inverse in Theorem 3.1. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.18758)

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.18758/gen_2409_18758.py:30)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.18758/README.md:1)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.18758/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.18758/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.18758/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.18758/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Key results:

- All G1–G9 gates pass.
- Shipping preset: `p=131071`, 33 polynomial terms.
- Bare oracle result: `0/3` solved—verdict `hardened`.
- Reference interpolation: about 129,567 operations versus 119 for the theorem route.
- Guess resistance: `0/200,000`.
- Answer size: 690 characters, approximately 173 tokens, 99 atomic values.
- G9 diagnostic: bare `0/3`, hinted `1/3`, placebo `2/3`; the README records that the hint showed no positive effect over placebo.
- No submission, commit, or push was performed.
